# .trivyignore — Trivy false-positive suppressions for Dex Trove
#
# Format: one suppression per line.
#   - Vulnerability ID (e.g. CVE-2024-XXXX) suppresses that specific CVE.
#   - Secret rule ID suppresses that secret type globally.
#   - Add a comment explaining every suppression.
#
# Scope note: the blocking gate runs with `--skip-dirs trove`. trove/ is redistributed upstream *content*
# (instructions, reference docs, example code); Dex never installs or executes it. It is scanned separately,
# non-blocking, and uploaded to the Security tab. Dex's own learn-time guards exclude real-format credentials
# and record Ananke-scanner placeholder hits as `secret_flags` (see docs/concepts/security-model.md).
#
# The .env file holds local PyPI upload tokens (UV_PUBLISH_TOKEN*). It is gitignored and never committed;
# CI uses OIDC Trusted Publishing and never sees it.
